--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The code — Apache-2.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under `src/`, `tests/` and `scripts/`, except as noted in (3).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. The dataset — CC0-1.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The published benchmark (audio, transcripts, metadata, per-utterance metrics):

    https://huggingface.co/datasets/nineninesix/multilingual-speech-benchmark

CC0-1.0, matching its source. The audio is derived from Common Voice 17.0
(https://commonvoice.mozilla.org), released under CC0-1.0 by Mozilla
Foundation. No audio is redistributed in this repository.

The generated reports under `reports/` describe that dataset and are CC0-1.0
with it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Vendored third-party code — MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    src/msbench/sim/_vendor/ecapa_tdnn.py

Vendored from microsoft/UniSpeech
(downstreams/speaker_verification/models/ecapa_tdnn.py), MIT licensed,
Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. Parts of it derive in turn from
https://github.com/lawlict/ECAPA-TDNN.

It is the model definition that the `wavlm_large_finetune.pth` checkpoint was
trained with — the checkpoint the stock seed-tts-eval scripts use for speaker
similarity — and is vendored rather than reimplemented so that numbers reported
under the `wavlm_ft` encoder come from the same architecture as the published
literature. It carries one documented change from upstream, recorded in the
file's own header.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Models and checkpoints
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The pipeline downloads pretrained models at runtime. They are not redistributed
here and each carries its own licence and terms:

    openai/whisper-large-v3                 Apache-2.0
    facebook/mms-1b-all                     CC-BY-NC-4.0  (non-commercial)
    ai-sage/GigaAM-Multilingual             MIT
    microsoft/wavlm-base-plus-sv            no licence declared on the model card
    microsoft/UniSpeech wavlm_large_finetune.pth   MIT (the UniSpeech repository)
    speechbrain/spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb       Apache-2.0
    ElevenLabs Scribe v2                    commercial API, ElevenLabs terms

Two of these need care rather than a glance:

  * MMS-1B-all is CC-BY-NC-4.0. Reporting its numbers is fine; a commercial
    pipeline that runs it inherits the non-commercial restriction.
  * microsoft/wavlm-base-plus-sv declares no licence on its model card. It is
    the encoder v1 used and is kept for continuity, but `wavlm_ft` and `ecapa`
    are the encoders this benchmark recommends, and both are clearly licensed.
